<title>GREECE: Drachma down vs most other euro currencies in Nov.</title>
<headline>Drachma down vs most other euro currencies in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The drachma eased versus most other EU currencies month-on-month in November but firmed against the U.S. dollar and the yen based on average fixing prices, Ionian research said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>		     Mo/Mo     Nov 96/Dec 95	Yr/Yr</p>
<p>		    (Currencies against the drachma)</p>
<p>    USD	    -0.66%	  0.17%	     1.94%</p>
<p>    ECU	     0.74%	 -0.23%	    -0.08%</p>
<p>    DEM	     0.48%	 -4.54%	    -4.49%</p>
<p>    FRF	     0.12%	 -2.82%	    -2.64%</p>
<p>    GBP	     4.16%	  8.23%	     8.41%</p>
<p>    ITL	     0.11%	  5.48%	     7.34%</p>
<p>    NLG	     0.50%	 -4.71%	    -4.63%</p>
<p>    YEN	    -0.52%	 -9.21%	    -7.54%</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
